WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:05.050
In Montreal, your French page shows the
line you added this week in English.

2
00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:09.430
Your build script runs next build alone,
so the line was never translated.

3
00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:15.640
General Translation keeps translations
current when your CI runs npx gt translate

4
00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:16.690
before the build.

5
00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:23.950
Create an API key for CI with the file,
context and translation queue permissions.

6
00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:28.930
Store it and your project ID
as secrets in your CI provider.

7
00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:33.910
Add npx gt translate to your build
script, before the build command.

8
00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:39.350
Run that build on every push to main, for
example with a GitHub Actions workflow.

9
00:00:39.860 --> 00:00:44.450
Each build then ships current translations
in Spanish, Japanese and French.
